#~ msgid "Lets Google reCAPTCHA, hCaptcha and Cloudflare Turnstile load before consent, as protection of the forms a visitor submits. Whether that counts as strictly necessary depends on your legal advice: in some countries reCAPTCHA is expected to wait for consent because it sends data to Google. If you switch this off, these services are blocked like any other provider until the visitor accepts their category, so <strong>forms protected by them will not submit before consent</strong>. Also remove any CAPTCHA entries from Script Blocking Exceptions above, which always win."
